    "pdpPlainTextPreview": "A sought-after, celebratory edition of The Sovereign\nWE ARE STRENGTHENING ACCOUNT SECURITY AND PROTECTING YOUR ACCESS WITH 2 STEP VERIFICATION. FIND OUT MORE Home Sovereign All Sovereign Coins 2012 Elizabeth II 'Diamond Jubilee' Sovereign Share via SOVEREIGN OF THE MONTH Gold Bullion 2012 Elizabeth II 'Diamond Jubilee' Sovereign Extremely Fine Condition Price: £995.00 EMAIL ME WHEN IN STOCK Email Me When In Stock PRODUCT CODE: HISSOV2012 A sought-after, celebratory edition of The Sovereign Struck in 2012 – the Diamond Jubilee year of Queen Elizabeth II Features a rare change of reverse design for this year only British sculptor Paul Day has created an alternative portrayal of St George and the dragon on the reverse The fourth coinage portrait of Elizabeth II by Ian Rank-Broadley adorns the coin’s obverse Selected as Sovereign of the Month Gold Bullion Read the full description YOU MIGHT ALSO BE INTERESTED IN ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Coin £62.51 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2022 1 oz Silver Bullion Coin £61.31 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 5 Genius Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Gold Bullion Coin £3,484.92 In Stock ADD TO BASKET 100th Anniversary of the Birth of Queen Elizabeth II 2026 UK £5 Brilliant Uncirculated Coin £17.50 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 2026 1oz Silver Bullion Twenty-Five Coin Tube £1,482.75 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 4 Mastermind Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Britannia 1g Gold Bullion Minted Bar £140.70 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 3 Decoder Medal £9.95 In Stock ADD TO BASKET Level 2 Explorer Medal and Collector Folder £9.95 In Stock Queen Elizabeth II's historic reign was celebrated with multiple jubilees, with the Diamond Jubilee in 2012 being a notable milestone. To commemorate this momentous occasion, The Royal Mint issued a special edition of The Sovereign featuring a rare alteration to its reverse design. This 2012 Diamond Jubilee Sovereign showcased a unique interpretation of the classic St George and the dragon motif, created by Paul Day specifically for the jubilee. This departure from the traditional design makes the 2012 Sovereign a particularly significant piece for collectors of this renowned gold coin, often referred to as \"the chief coin of the world\". The Diamond Jubilee marked 60 years since Queen Elizabeth II's accession to the throne in 1952. It was a remarkable achievement, with Elizabeth II being only the second British monarch to reach this milestone, following Queen Victoria's Diamond Jubilee in 1897. Collectors and numismatists should take note of this special Sovereign, as it represents an opportunity to acquire a coin that not only commemorates a historic royal event but also features a unique design in the long-standing Sovereign series. Created in 1816 for the introduction of the modern Sovereign, Benedetto Pistrucci’s St George and the dragon design has become intrinsically linked with the ‘chief coin of the world’. This is not just due to Pistrucci’s masterful artistry, but due to its repeated use on the reverse of the coin. Deviations from Pistrucci’s design tend to only happen to commemorate significant royal events, so it is perhaps not surprising that The Sovereign has featured several special, one-year-only designs during the extensive reign of Elizabeth II. A Remarkable Monarch Born on 21 April 1926, Elizabeth II was third in line to the British throne behind her uncle Edward, Prince of Wales (later Edward VIII) and her father, the Duke of York (later George VI). However, her uncle’s abdication in 1936 changed the course of history and her father became king; on 6 February 1952, upon her father’s death, Elizabeth II acceded to the throne. Prior to her accession, she committed herself to public service, declaring in a speech as Princess Elizabeth, ‘I declare before you all that my whole life, whether it be long or short, shall be devoted to your service’. It was a promise the monarch upheld throughout her record-bre"
